#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""vmctl -- host-side controller for the multi-head desktop test VMs.

Builds golden images (cloud-init + a desktop metapackage, autologin of user
`test`: GNOME/Wayland via GDM, Plasma/Wayland via SDDM, Xfce/X11 via LightDM,
sway via greetd) and runs instances of them under QEMU/KVM with a
virtio-vga whose heads are hot-plugged/resized from the host over QEMU's
D-Bus display backend.  Screenshots come out of QMP `screendump`.

Python 3 stdlib only; shells out to qemu-system-x86_64, qemu-img,
cloud-localds, dbus-daemon, gdbus, ssh, scp, ssh-keygen.

State lives under $VMDATA (default ~/vm-data):
  golden/<flavor>.qcow2                golden image (qcow2 overlay on the
                                       base cloud image in $VMIMAGES, by
                                       absolute path -- the golden does NOT
                                       depend on any build/instance dir; an
                                       ISO flavor's golden has no backing
                                       file at all, see build-iso-golden.sh)
  golden/<flavor>-packages.txt         dpkg list of the finished image
  golden/<flavor>.build.log            serial log of the build VM
  instances/<name>/{disk.qcow2,seed.img,qmp.sock,bus,dbus.pid,
                    qemu.pid,serial.log,meta.json}
  keys/id_ed25519[.pub]                guest root ssh key, generated once
See vm/README.md for the QEMU/D-Bus facts this relies on.
"""
