# session is "active" a few seconds before anything is drawn; on a slow host a
# screenshot taken right away still shows the kernel console.  Verdicts:
# PAINTED, WAIT <why>, or UNKNOWN (nothing in the guest to go by: the caller
# then watches head 0's screendump for a change).
pg() {   # pgrep -x, plus the name nixpkgs' wrapper leaves in /proc/comm
  # A wrapped GUI program's comm is `.NAME-wrapped` truncated to fifteen characters:
  # measured on the live NixOS guest as `.swaybg-wrapped` (exactly fifteen) and
  # `.wdotool-wrappe`, while sway's own comm stays `sway` because its wrapper execs the
  # unwrapped binary [recon2/nixos].  The truncation is BUILT here rather than guessed
  # at with a `-wr.*` suffix: for a 12- or 13-character name -- kwin_wayland,
  # budgie-panel, cosmic-panel, mate-session, lxqt-session, every one of them a shell=
  # or compositor= of some DESKTOPS row -- fifteen characters leave no `-wr` at all
  # (`.kwin_wayland-w`), and a suffix pattern matched none of them.  `.` plus the first
